content.text:
@electron/asar 4.3.1 installed in the workspace. Now write a Node script that:
1. Lists asar files matching dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings-{general,models}/*, and @deepseek-ai/dsh/lib/plugin*.js, bin.js
2. Extracts client.js from both settings packages, computes sha256
3. Prints package.json versions for both
4. Also extracts the dsh plugin command file to a workspace file for reading.

extractFile signature: asar.extractFile(archive, filename) → Buffer. In 4.x it's promise-based? @electron/asar API: `asar.extractFile(archive, filename)` returns Buffer synchronously? In v3+, extractFile is async (returns Promise<Buffer>)? Let me check: @electron/asar v3 changed to promises: extractFile(archive, filename): Promise<Buffer>. Also listPackage(archive): Promise<string[]>. I'll write async code accordingly.

Script:
```js
const asar = require('@electron/asar');
const fs = require('fs');
const crypto = require('crypto');
(async () => {
  const archive = 'D:/deepseek harness/resources/app.asar';
  const files = await asar.listPackage(archive);
  const match = (re) => files.filter(f => re.test(f));
  console.log('--- settings-general files ---');
  console.log(match(/dsh\/node_modules\/@deepseek-ai\/dsh-client-ui-settings-general\//).join('\n'));
  console.log('--- settings-models files ---');
  console.log(match(/dsh\/node_modules\/@deepseek-ai\/dsh-client-ui-settings-models\//).join('\n'));
  console.log('--- dsh core lib files ---');
  console.log(match(/^dsh\/node_modules\/@deepseek-ai\/dsh\/lib\//).join('\n'));
  for (const pkg of ['dsh-client-ui-settings-general','dsh-client-ui-settings-models']) {
    const pj = await asar.extractFile(archive, `dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/${pkg}/package.json`);
    const meta = JSON.parse(pj.toString('utf8'));
    console.log(pkg, 'version=', meta.version);
    const client = await asar.extractFile(archive, `dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/${pkg}/lib/client.js`);
    const sha = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(client).digest('hex');
    console.log(pkg, 'client.js sha256=', sha, 'bytes=', client.length);
  }
})().catch(e => { console.error(e); process.exit(1); });
```

Also save the dsh plugin file + bin.js + package.json of @deepseek-ai/dsh to disk for reading:
```js
for (const rel of [...]) fs.writeFileSync(...)
```
I'll first list, then in the same script extract copies into workspace (writes in workspace ✓).

Let me write this script to a file and run with bundled node (require resolution from asar-tools dir — use workdir asar-tools or NODE_PATH; simpler: put script in asar-tools and run node script.js from there).

